-- | Places numeric ticks at round values (default on) instead of six evenly spaced ticks across the range, in the spirit of R\'s @pretty()@.
--
-- The step is 1, 2, or 5 times a power of ten, chosen as the \"nice number\" nearest a fifth of the visible range (Heckbert\'s rule), and ticks are its multiples inside the range. That gives about four to seven ticks, close to R\'s @pretty()@: a padded range of -0.365 to 7.665 gets ticks at 0, 2, 4 and 6. Custom tick labels take precedence. The background grid follows the ticks.
