-- | Builds a pie chart with one wedge per value, like R\'s @pie(x, labels = names, col = colors, clockwise = TRUE)@.
--
-- Wedge i spans the fraction values\[i\] \/ sum(values) of the circle. Wedges start at 12 o\'clock and run clockwise (R\'s default starts at 3 o\'clock and runs counter-clockwise). Each wedge is a filled unit-radius polygon with 24 arc segments. Names, when given, are drawn at radius 1.15 beside the middle of each wedge\'s arc and also label the wedges, so the automatic legend lists them. Colors are recycled; empty uses an 8-color built-in palette starting blue, red, green. The axes and grid are hidden and both ranges are fixed at \[-1.4, 1.4\]. The pie is drawn in data units, so it is round only when the plotting area is square, e.g. @.size(598, 640)@ with the default margins; the default 960x640 canvas draws an ellipse.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > auto plt = dm::Plot::pie({3.0, 2.0, 1.0}, {"rent", "food", "fun"}).size(598, 640);
-- > std::print("{}\n", plt.series().size());  // 6
-- > plt.save("budget.svg");
