-- | Builds a normal Q-Q plot: the sorted @data@ against standard-normal quantiles, like R\'s @qqnorm(y)@.
--
-- The i-th smallest value (i = 1..n) is plotted against the normal quantile of the plotting position (i - 0.5) \/ n. R\'s @ppoints()@ uses that rule only for n \> 10 and (i - 3\/8) \/ (n + 1\/4) for n \<= 10, so the x coordinates differ from R for small samples. Points that fall on a straight line indicate normally distributed data; add the reference line with qqline(). The title is \"Normal Q-Q\", the axis labels \"Theoretical Quantiles\" and \"Sample Quantiles\".
