-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- ImageLoader

-- | A configurable, disk-backed batch iterator over a standard image dataset.
--
-- Datasets: \"mnist\" and \"fashion\_mnist\" (28x28 grayscale, 10 classes; 60000 train \/ 10000 test), \"cifar10\" (32x32 RGB, 10 classes; 50000 \/ 10000) and \"cifar100\" (32x32 RGB, 100 fine or 20 coarse classes; 50000 \/ 10000).
--
-- Iteration works in epochs. has\_next()\/next() walk the current epoch\'s order; reset() starts the next epoch (with a fresh shuffle when shuffling is on). Every setter returns the loader for chaining and rewinds the current epoch, so configure before iterating.
--
-- Reading is const and opens files per call, so batch()\/take() may be called from several threads at once; next()\/reset() and the setters mutate and must not race.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::datasets::ImageLoader test("cifar10", "test");
-- > test.set_batch_size(500).set_layout("nchw").set_normalize(false);
-- > const auto first = test.next();          // shape {500, 3, 32, 32}, values 0..255
-- > std::print("{}\n", test.class_names()[first.labels[0]]);   // "cat"
