-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fem1D

-- | Solve steady or transient one-dimensional divergence-form problems with P1 Galerkin FEM. Models -(p/u\')\'+q/u=f and u\_t-(p/u\')\'+q/u=f on a caller-supplied mesh. Requires at least two finite strictly increasing nodes, finite coefficient\/ boundary\/source data and finite assembled arithmetic with nonzero Thomas pivots; those mathematical\/geometry preconditions are not fully validated. Positive p, nonnegative q\/Robin data and adequate constraints give the usual coercive model. Piecewise-constant p\/q can be scalar or one per element. Results own their values; input mesh\/data are unchanged. Calls share no mutable global state, while callback side effects\/concurrency belong to the caller.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
-- > std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
--
-- __References__
--
-- * MFEM, Weak Formulations: https:\/\/mfem.org\/fem\_weak\_form\/ . This native implementation uses P1 intervals, three-point Gauss-Legendre loads and a tridiagonal direct solve.
