-- | Solve the steady P1 system for -(p/u\')\'+q/u=f with endpoint boundary data. Follows FEM1D\'s mesh\/coefficient\/finite-arithmetic\/nonsingular-pivot preconditions. Uses three-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature of f times each local basis, natural boundary terms and symmetric Dirichlet elimination, then Thomas elimination. O(N) work\/storage for N nodes; invokes the source three times per element. No callback pointer is retained. Independent calls share no mutable state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > struct Unit final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 1;}} source;
-- > const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{});
-- > std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
--
-- __References__
--
-- * https:\/\/mfem.org\/fem\_weak\_form\/ ; native interval P1 and quadrature choices as FEM1D.
--
-- C++: @FEM1DResult datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector\<double\> & p, const std::vector\<double\> & q, ScalarField1D & f, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: If p\/q are empty or have the wrong lengths.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.AllocationError') for C++ @std::bad\_alloc@: If assembly\/result storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate.
--
-- See also: @solve\_builtin@, @solve\_transient@.
fem1DSolve
  :: (IsMesh1D a, IsScalarField1D b, IsBoundaryCondition1D c, IsBoundaryCondition1D d)
  => a  -- ^ Borrowed mesh with at least two finite strictly increasing nodes.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed diffusion coefficient: length1 or one per element.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed reaction coefficient: length1 or one per element.
  -> b  -- ^ Borrowed spatial source; evaluate() may have caller-owned side effects.
  -> c  -- ^ Left endpoint condition, with outward normal -1.
  -> d  -- ^ Right endpoint condition, with outward normal +1.
  -> P.IO Fem1DResult  -- ^ Owned original nodes and computed nodal values.
fem1DSolve _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 _x5 _x6 = R.call 917 [R.object _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.object _x4, R.object _x5, R.object _x6] P.>>= R.result

-- | Solve the steady system using an owned named spatial source, without a director callback. Shares the live-source solver and its mathematical\/precondition\/storage contracts. Sources: zero=0 (params unused); constant=c ({1}); linear=m/x+c ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params\[i\]/x^i) (empty gives0); sine=A/sin(w/x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Missing trailing parameters use those defaults; extra parameters are ignored except polynomial, which uses all entries. Name matching is exact\/case-sensitive.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{}, {},{});
-- > std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
--
-- __References__
--
-- * https:\/\/mfem.org\/fem\_weak\_form\/ ; source definitions are native convenience choices.
--
-- C++: @FEM1DResult datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve\_builtin(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector\<double\> & p, const std::vector\<double\> & q, const std::string & source, const std::vector\<double\> & source\_params, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: For an unknown source or malformed p\/q lengths.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.AllocationError') for C++ @std::bad\_alloc@: If owned parameter\/assembly\/result storage cannot be allocated.
--
-- See also: @solve@, @solve\_transient\_builtin@.
fem1DSolveBuiltin
  :: (IsMesh1D a, IsBoundaryCondition1D b, IsBoundaryCondition1D c)
  => a  -- ^ Borrowed valid finite interval mesh; unchanged.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed scalar\/per-element diffusion coefficient.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed scalar\/per-element reaction coefficient.
  -> P.String  -- ^ Exact name zero, constant, linear, polynomial or sine.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed positional source parameters, with defaults described above.
  -> b  -- ^ Left endpoint data using outward normal -1.
  -> c  -- ^ Right endpoint data using outward normal +1.
  -> P.IO Fem1DResult  -- ^ Owned computed nodal result, retaining no source or input reference.
fem1DSolveBuiltin _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 _x5 _x6 _x7 = R.call 918 [R.object _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.toCpp _x4, R.toCpp _x5, R.object _x6, R.object _x7] P.>>= R.result

-- | Integrate u\_t-(p/u\')\'+q/u=f with P1 space and actual backward-Euler time intervals. Shares FEM1D\'s spatial\/finite-arithmetic\/nonzero-pivot preconditions. Source and boundary data represent a time-independent model; the live callback is actually reevaluated three times per element at every time advance, not cached. Stores initial u0 as supplied, then imposes boundary data at later solves. Nominal step dt is shortened at t\_end; actual positive time differences enter the mass term. Stops once t\_end is reached, avoiding a duplicate rounded last time even when ceil(t\_end\/dt) overestimates the number of advances. O(S\*N) work\/output storage for S advances\/N nodes, O(N) assembly temporaries; no optional trace or quota. Backward Euler is unconditionally stable for the coercive semidiscrete model, not a guarantee of arbitrary-step accuracy or finite arithmetic for arbitrary parameters. Input arrays remain unchanged; callback exceptions\/side effects\/concurrent safety belong to caller.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > struct Zero final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 0;}} source;
-- > const auto t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{},{0,1,0},.5,.5);
-- > std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2 0.142857
--
-- __References__
--
-- * Arnold (2012), Numerical Analysis of Partial Differential Equations, chapter5 section2. https:\/\/www-users.cse.umn.edu\/~arnold\/8445.f12\/notes.pdf . Native load quadrature, fixed data and rounded\/shortened time grid are implementation choices.
--
-- C++: @FEM1DTimeSeries datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve\_transient(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector\<double\> & p, const std::vector\<double\> & q, ScalarField1D & f, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right, const std::vector\<double\> & u0, double t\_end, double dt)@
