-- See also: @solve\_transient\_builtin@, 'Fem1DTimeSeries'.
fem1DSolveTransient
  :: (IsMesh1D a, IsScalarField1D b, IsBoundaryCondition1D c, IsBoundaryCondition1D d)
  => a  -- ^ Borrowed valid mesh with at least two finite increasing nodes.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed scalar\/per-element diffusion coefficient.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed scalar\/per-element reaction coefficient.
  -> b  -- ^ Borrowed spatial callback, reevaluated at every advance.
  -> c  -- ^ Fixed left condition, with outward normal -1.
  -> d  -- ^ Fixed right condition, with outward normal +1.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Borrowed finite initial nodal values, exactly one per mesh node.
  -> P.Double  -- ^ Positive finite final time, in time units.
  -> P.Double  -- ^ Positive finite nominal time step in the same units; may exceed t\_end.
  -> P.IO Fem1DTimeSeries  -- ^ Owned nodes, initial state and strictly advancing slices ending at t\_end.
fem1DSolveTransient _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 _x5 _x6 _x7 _x8 _x9 = R.call 919 [R.object _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.object _x4, R.object _x5, R.object _x6, R.toCpp _x7, R.toCpp _x8, R.toCpp _x9] P.>>= R.result

-- | Integrate the same backward-Euler model with a named source and no callback subclass. Uses the same private source construction as solve\_builtin() and the same actual time loop as solve\_transient(); no second solver or per-language glue. Names\/defaults: zero=0; constant=c ({1}); linear=m/x+c ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params\[i\]/x^i) (empty0); sine=A/sin(w/x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Extra entries ignored except polynomial; exact case-sensitive names. Source objects are local and synchronous; results own values, not callback aliases. All spatial\/time\/initial-state, complexity and stability contracts follow solve\_transient(); ordinary output has no optional history\/quota.
