-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- KalmanFilter

-- | Owned fixed-model linear covariance Kalman filter with optional full RTS smoothing. Models x\_k=F/x\_(k-1)+w and z\_k=H/x\_k+v with caller-supplied Q\/R covariance. Inputs are copied; predict\/update mutate this instance, independent copies evolve separately. Concurrent mutation requires synchronization. Shape checks do not establish finite values, covariance PSD, noise independence or valid probability assumptions: those remain caller preconditions. Uses explicit LU inverses and simplified covariance updates, not a Joseph\/square-root method. Under a valid linear Gaussian model the mean is conditional MMSE; floating output is approximate. No universal realized-error or numerical PSD guarantee.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::filter::KalmanFilter k({{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{{3}},{0},{{4}});
-- > k.predict();k.update({2});std::print("{}\n",k.state()[0]); // 1.25
