toKalmanFilter = R.wrapHandle P.. R.objectHandle

-- | Copy a fixed linear model and initial state, validating matrix dimensions. No finite\/covariance-definiteness checks are added; the caller supplies statistically valid finite matrices and invertible required innovation\/prediction covariances. O(n/n+m/n+m\*m) copied model\/state storage for n state and m observation dimensions.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const dm::filter::KalmanFilter k({{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{0},{{2}});
-- > std::print("{}\n",k.covariance()[0][0]); // 2
--
-- C++: @datamunge::filter::KalmanFilter::KalmanFilter(std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> F, std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> H, std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> Q, std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> R, std::vector\<double\> x0, std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> P0)@
