-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: On ragged\/incompatible matrix shapes.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.AllocationError') for C++ @std::bad\_alloc@: On model\/state allocation failure.
newKalmanFilter
  :: [[P.Double]]  -- ^ Owned n-by-n transition matrix.
  -> [[P.Double]]  -- ^ Owned m-by-n observation matrix.
  -> [[P.Double]]  -- ^ Owned n-by-n process covariance.
  -> [[P.Double]]  -- ^ Owned m-by-m observation covariance.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Owned initial length-n state mean.
  -> [[P.Double]]  -- ^ Owned initial n-by-n state covariance.
  -> P.IO KalmanFilter
newKalmanFilter _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 _x5 _x6 =
  P.fmap KalmanFilter' (R.construct 1056 P.Nothing [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.toCpp _x4, R.toCpp _x5, R.toCpp _x6])

-- | Predict x=F/x and P=F/P\*F^T+Q once, mutating the current state. Matrix arithmetic is ordinary floating point; nonfinite results propagate. O(n^3) dense work\/O(n^2) temporaries; no rollback guarantee on exceptions.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::filter::KalmanFilter k({{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{2},{{4}});k.predict();
-- > std::print("{}\n",k.covariance()[0][0]); // 5
--
-- C++: @void datamunge::filter::KalmanFilter::predict()@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.AllocationError') for C++ @std::bad\_alloc@: On temporary allocation failure.
