-- See also: @update@.
kalmanFilterPredict
  :: IsKalmanFilter a
  => a  -- ^ the object
  -> P.IO ()
kalmanFilterPredict _self = R.call 1050 [R.object _self] P.>>= R.result

-- | Correct from z using innovation covariance, LU gain and simplified posterior covariance. Computes y=z-H/x,S=H/P/H^T+R,K=P/H^T/S^-1, then x+=K/y and P=(I-K/H)/P. Requires finite statistically valid inputs\/invertible S; shape validation alone does not ensure those properties. Rounding may lose symmetry\/PSD; not Joseph form. Mutates state without rollback guarantee.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::filter::KalmanFilter k({{1}},{{1}},{{1}},{{3}},{0},{{5}});k.update({2});
-- > std::print("{}\n",k.state()[0]); // 1.25
