-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- KdTree2D

-- | Own a balanced alternating-axis median tree for planar nearest\/k\/radius queries. Finite points required. Stable deterministic build ties use other coordinate, then original input index; each node retains original identity. Nearest and k-nearest equal computed distances prefer earliest input index, including duplicates. Distances use widened coordinate subtraction and hypot, avoiding the old double square overflow\/underflow; they remain rounded machine values. Construction expected O(n log(n+1)) work\/O(n) owned storage; tree height O(log n). Queries can visit every node: no universal average O(log n) guarantee without distribution assumptions. No insertion\/removal. Const queries use local state and share no mutable state; original caller data are not retained.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const dm::geometry::KDTree2D tree({{0,0},{3,4}});
-- > std::print("{}\n",tree.nearest({1,0}).x); // 0
