-- | Integrate one complete checked forward initial-value problem. Complete finite nonempty y0 and finite forward span t\_end\>t\_start with representable difference are checked before callbacks. Known method, finite positive step\/abs\_tol, finite rel\_tol\>=0 and max\_step\>=0 are validated, including inactive numeric controls. Each callback receives a finite fixed-dimensional stage and must return finite matching dimension; exceptions propagate. Steps must advance representable time; tiny\/nonadvancing steps throw rather than loop. No absolute1e-14 endpoint skip; successful output reaches t\_end. Adams uses original RK4 startup and clamped order2..4; a shortened final step uses RK4 instead of applying constant-grid coefficients to unequal spacing. RK45 does not reuse FSAL and accepts only scaled error\<=1, not a tiny-step bypass. Local error control is not a certified global error, stability or energy bound. State\/control\/input references are not retained. Callback effects before a later error\/quota failure persist; no partial solution\/trace is returned. Default work policies:1000000 attempts,7000000 RHS calls,1000000 retained solution scalar entries; limits overloads allow0 to disable each policy.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > struct F:dm::ode::RHS{std::vector<double>evaluate(double,const std::vector<double>&y)override{return {-y[0]};}};F f;dm::ode::ODESolver s({dm::ode::StepMethod::Euler,4,.25});std::print("{}\n",s.solve(f,{1.},0.,.25).y.back()[0]); // 0.75
--
-- __References__
