-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- AdaGrad

-- | AdaGrad on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface. Accumulates squared full gradients; divides each update by sqrt(sum+epsilon). Tests the pre-update gradient norm after applying the update. Every optimize call resets the accumulator. O(p) local storage. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
