-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- AugmentedLagrangian

-- | AugmentedLagrangian on the EqualityConstrainedFunction callback interface. Uses fixed inner gradient steps on f+lambda/c+rho/||c||^2\/2, capped so each displacement norm is at most one. Updates multipliers after each inner budget and doubles rho until feasibility tolerance or outer budget. No dual-stationarity test is exposed. Objective return alone is not a KKT certificate. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const dm::optim::AugmentedLagrangian optimizer;
-- > std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_outer_iterations); // 50
--
-- __References__
--
-- * J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization, second edition, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-0-387-40065-5. The implemented variant and stopping rules are specified above.
