-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- DifferentialEvolution

-- | DifferentialEvolution on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface. Box-constrained differential mutation\/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1\/best1\/current\_to\_best1\/rand2 and binomial\/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population\_size\*p) storage; no global certificate. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
