-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fista

-- | FISTA on the ProximalFunction callback interface. Classical t recurrence (1+sqrt(1+4\*t^2))\/2 and extrapolated gradient points, followed by the supplied proximal map. Stops on successive accepted-coordinate displacement. No adaptive restart, backtracking or monotonicity safeguard. Supply the correct proximal dimensions and a rate at most 1\/L for the standard convex bound. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const dm::optim::FISTA optimizer;
-- > std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 10000
--
-- __References__
--
-- * A. Beck and M. Teboulle (2009), A Fast Iterative Shrinkage-Thresholding Algorithm for Linear Inverse Problems, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1137\/080716542
--
-- The C++ class @datamunge::optim::FISTA@.
--
-- A value holds the C++ object; it is released when garbage collection reclaims the last value holding it, or by 'R.closeObject'.
