-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- InteriorPoint

-- | InteriorPoint on the InequalityConstrainedFunction callback interface. Gradient steps on f-mu\*sum(log(-c)) with c\<0. Backtracks only for strict feasibility, not barrier-objective decrease, then decays mu after each fixed inner budget. Requires a strictly feasible start and can fail later when feasible steps underflow. No KKT or barrier-stationarity stop test; no phase-I feasibility search. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
