-- | Return the joint noise-free posterior over ordered query points. Observation noise conditions the training fit and is excluded from query covariance. Identical queries have the same latent variable. An empty query list after fitting gives an empty posterior.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::optim::RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate gp(1.0, 0.1);
-- > gp.fit({{0.0}}, {1.0});
-- > const auto joint = gp.joint_posterior({{0.2}, {0.4}});
-- > std::print("{}\n", joint.covariance.size()); // 4
--
-- C++: @GaussianJointPosterior datamunge::optim::RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate::joint\_posterior(const std::vector\<std::vector\<double\>\> & queries) const@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.NativeError') for C++ @std::logic\_error@: The model has yet to be fitted.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: A query has nonfinite coordinates or the wrong shape.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.LengthError') for C++ @std::length\_error@: Posterior matrix size exceeds representable range.
--
-- See also: @predict@, @joint\_bayesian\_search@.
rbfGaussianProcessSurrogateJointPosterior
  :: IsRbfGaussianProcessSurrogate a
