-- | Run Nadam from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Fixed-beta Nadam variant: direction beta1/m\/(1-beta1^t)+(1-beta1)/g\/(1-beta1^t), divided by sqrt(v\/(1-beta2^t))+epsilon. Does not implement scheduled momentum products. Tests the gradient used after updating; O(p) reset state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
-- > dm::optim::NadamOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
-- > std::vector<double> x{0,0};
-- > const auto value=dm::optim::Nadam(controls).optimize(f,x);
-- > std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
--
-- C++: @double datamunge::optim::Nadam::optimize(DifferentiableFunction & function, std::vector\<double\> & coordinates) const@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Nadam: step\_size must be positive; Nadam: beta1 must be in \[0, 1); Nadam: beta2 must be in \[0, 1); Nadam: epsilon must be positive; Nadam: tolerance must be non-negative.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.NativeError') for C++ @std::exception@: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.
--
-- See also: @trace\_optimize@, 'NadamOptions'.
nadamOptimize
  :: (IsNadam a, IsDifferentiableFunction b)
  => a  -- ^ the object
  -> b  -- ^ Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite output shapes.
  -> IORef.IORef [P.Double]  -- ^ Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.; C++ writes it back
  -> P.IO P.Double  -- ^ Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
nadamOptimize _self _x1 _x2 = do
  _v2 <- IORef.readIORef _x2
  _reply <- R.call 1985 [R.object _self, R.object _x1, R.slot 0 _v2]
  R.writeBack _reply 0 _x2
  R.result _reply

