-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Newton

-- | Newton on the HessianFunction callback interface. Adds fixed damping to the supplied Hessian diagonal, solves with partial-pivot Gaussian elimination, and takes a full step. This is not a globalised line-search method; indefinite or nearly singular Hessians can increase the loss or produce huge steps. Stops on gradient norm. Dense O(p^3) solve\/O(p^2) storage. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
