-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pso

-- | PSO on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface. Box-constrained particle swarm with global or ring attraction and constant or linearly decayed inertia. Coordinates seed one clamped particle; returns the best visited feasible point. Stops after more than twenty small-best-improvement iterations or its budget. O(population\_size\*p) storage; no global-optimality certificate. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
