-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent

-- | RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface. Randomly permutes coordinates each epoch and visits consecutive blocks once. Full-gradient block directions use Armijo backtracking and restore a failed block. This is random reshuffling, not independent coordinate draws. Stops on the full epoch-end gradient norm; O(p) local storage. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
