-- | @n@ colours of the viridis scale, from dark purple through blue and green to yellow, matching R\'s @viridisLite::viridis(n)@ at n = 10.
--
-- Viridis is perceptually uniform, so equal steps in value look like equal steps in colour, and it stays readable in greyscale and for the common forms of colour blindness. Colours are interpolated linearly between viridis(10)\'s ten anchors.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto pal = dm::graphics::viridis_colors(10);
-- > std::print("{} {} {}\n", pal[0].r, pal[5].g, pal[9].b);  // 68 158 37
--
-- __References__
--
-- * S. van der Walt and N. Smith (2015). \"mpl colourmaps\" (viridis): https:\/\/bids.github.io\/colormap\/
-- * viridisLite: https:\/\/sjmgarnier.github.io\/viridisLite\/
