-- | The Laplacian pyramid: for every level except the last, level\_i = (Gaussian level i) minus (Gaussian level i+1 upsampled back to level i\'s size) -- the detail lost by blurring+downsampling at that scale, re-centered at 128 (see detail::signed\_difference\_image()) so it stores as an ordinary image; the final level is the smallest Gaussian level kept as-is (the residual low-frequency image the whole pyramid was built from). Reconstructing the original from a Laplacian pyramid is the classical use (progressively add each un-recentered level back onto the upsampled reconstruction-so-far) but isn\'t implemented here -- this module only needed the decomposition direction.
