-- | Measure a supplied mesh and test every nonvertex site against every circle. Performs the structural checks on DelaunayAnalysis first. The complete prospective circle count faces\*(unique\_sites-3) is checked before circle queries; zero cap disables only that limit. O(n log(n+1)+f log(f+1)+fu) work and O(n+f) storage; minimum angles are floating diagnostics and are not certified bounds. This is a local property analysis, not a global embedding\/coverage certificate.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> p{{0,0},{1,0},{1,1},{0,1}};
-- > const auto a=dm::geometry::delaunay_analyze(p,dm::geometry::delaunay_triangulation(p));
-- > std::print("{} {} {}\n",a.edges,a.boundary_edges,a.circle_tests); // 5 4 2
--
-- Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: @max\_tests@ = @1000000@.
--
-- C++: @DelaunayAnalysis datamunge::geometry::delaunay\_analyze(const std::vector\<Point2D\> & points, const std::vector\<Triangle\> & triangles, std::size\_t max\_tests = 1000000)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Nonfinite coordinates, bad\/degenerate\/non-CCW\/duplicate faces or nonmanifold edges.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.LengthError') for C++ @std::length\_error@: Circle-count arithmetic or optional cap exceeded.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.AllocationError') for C++ @std::bad\_alloc@: Allocation fails.
--
-- See also: 'DelaunayAnalysis', 'delaunayTriangulation'.
delaunayAnalyze
  :: [Point2D]  -- ^ Finite original sites, unchanged.
  -> [Triangle]  -- ^ Finite CCW faces with valid original indices, unchanged.
  -> P.IO DelaunayAnalysis  -- ^ Owned scalar topology, actual query\/violation counts and approximate angle.
delaunayAnalyze _x1 _x2 = R.call 123 [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2] P.>>= R.result

-- | Measure a supplied mesh and test every nonvertex site against every circle. Performs the structural checks on DelaunayAnalysis first. The complete prospective circle count faces\*(unique\_sites-3) is checked before circle queries; zero cap disables only that limit. O(n log(n+1)+f log(f+1)+fu) work and O(n+f) storage; minimum angles are floating diagnostics and are not certified bounds. This is a local property analysis, not a global embedding\/coverage certificate.
