-- C++: @ClosestPairResult datamunge::geometry::closest\_pair(const std::vector\<Point2D\> & points)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: If point count is too small or any coordinate is nonfinite.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.LengthError') for C++ @std::length\_error@: If complete pair count cannot fit size\_t.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.ArithmeticError') for C++ @std::overflow\_error@: If arithmetic\/counters or the selected legacy distance cannot fit.
--
-- See also: @closest\_pair\_indexed@, @closest\_pair\_trace@.
closestPair
  :: [Point2D]  -- ^ Borrowed original finite planar coordinates, length at least two.
  -> P.IO ClosestPairResult  -- ^ Owned selected point copies and checked finite-double measured distance.
closestPair _x1 = R.call 129 [R.toCpp _x1] P.>>= R.result

-- | Compute Andrew\'s strict monotone-chain hull using exact binary64 orientation signs. Validates all coordinates before internal indexed copies or sorting; the original by-value argument copy occurs at the call boundary. Exact coordinate equality removes duplicates (including signed zero); the earliest matching original record supplies its representation. Returns lexicographic-minimum first, counterclockwise, no repeated endpoint and no collinear edge interiors. Empty\/singleton\/two-point\/collinear outputs follow ConvexHullAnalysis. O(n log n) comparisons plus O(n) bounded exact-sign tests, O(n) scratch\/output, no global state. The legacy by-value signature is retained and has no optional caps. Other geometry routines that use cross() retain their own floating contracts.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto h=dm::geometry::convex_hull({{0,0},{2,0},{2,2},{0,2},{1,1}});
-- > std::cout << h.size(); // 4
--
-- __References__
--
-- * A. M. Andrew (1979), Another efficient algorithm for convex hulls in two dimensions, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/0020-0190(79)90072-3 .
--
-- C++: @std::vector\<Point2D\> datamunge::geometry::convex\_hull(std::vector\<Point2D\> points)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Any nonfinite coordinate.
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.LengthError') for C++ @std::length\_error@: Work\/container size exhaustion.
--
-- See also: 'convexHullAnalyze', 'convexHullTrace', @orientation\_sign@.
convexHull
  :: [Point2D]  -- ^ Finite planar records, copied by value as in the original API.
  -> P.IO [Point2D]  -- ^ Owned strict hull of the represented coordinates.
convexHull _x1 = R.call 130 [R.toCpp _x1] P.>>= R.result

-- | Execute the same exact-sign hull kernel with identities and actual work. Same ordering, degeneracy and complexity contract as convex\_hull(). Full finite validation precedes the complete max\_points cap and scratch allocation. No events or completed-chain snapshots are retained; event cap is ignored.
--
-- __Example__
