-- See also: 'DtwResult', 'plotDtwAlignment'.
dtwPathCost
  :: [P.Double]  -- ^ Nonempty finite first sequence.
  -> [P.Double]  -- ^ Nonempty finite second sequence.
  -> [P.Int]  -- ^ Borrowed signed first indices, zero through a.size()-1.
  -> [P.Int]  -- ^ Borrowed parallel signed second indices, zero through b.size()-1.
  -> P.IO P.Double  -- ^ Finite forward-order sum of absolute differences on the supplied witness.
dtwPathCost _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 = R.call 138 [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.toCpp _x4] P.>>= R.result

-- | Draw two scalar series and their validated DTW correspondence segments natively. Costs use unshifted inputs; only drawing adds offset to a and subtracts it from b. Requires result.distance to equal the validated forward witness sum exactly; it does not independently prove optimality. Validates complete inputs\/witness, finite plotted coordinates and optional path-pair cap before drawing allocation. Owns all series; no file I\/O or model mutation. Concurrent calls share no state.
