-- C++: @double datamunge::geometry::discrete\_frechet\_distance(const std::vector\<Point2D\> & p, const std::vector\<Point2D\> & q)@
discreteFrechetDistance :: [Point2D] -> [Point2D] -> P.IO P.Double
discreteFrechetDistance _x1 _x2 = R.call 140 [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2] P.>>= R.result

-- | Compute a seeded incremental enclosing circle using three nested loops. Fixed MT19937-64 seed42 and std::shuffle preserve ordinary processing order on the same standard library. One\/two\/three-point boundary rebuilds use translated long-double geometry, exact orientation for collinearity, and overflow checks. Collinear triples use the farthest-pair diameter. Containment tolerance is1e-9\*max(1,radius), so the returned circle is a numerical approximation, not an exact enclosure\/minimality certificate. O(n^3) worst-case tests, O(n) copied driver storage. No expected-linear guarantee for this particular loop implementation or timing claim.
