-- | Triangulate a finite simple polygon using exact orientation-based ear decisions. Rejects duplicate vertices, zero area, overlapping adjacent edges and every nonadjacent edge intersection\/touch. A repeated closing vertex is a duplicate. Collinear forward boundary vertices are allowed. Uses the exact turn at the lexicographically least vertex for simple-polygon winding, avoiding area cancellation. O(n^2) validation and O(n^3) worst-case ear search, O(n) working storage. n\<3 returns empty after finite validation. For n=3 the historical vertex order is retained; larger clockwise rings are reversed internally. Input is borrowed unchanged; no references or mutable global state survive.
