-- | Find the farthest hull pair using actual rotating antipodes. Computes the canonical exact-orientation convex hull first, then advances a CCW antipodal pointer while the next point has strictly greater baseline area, using cross\_difference\_sign() without rounded cross-product subtraction. Tests both edge endpoints against the current antipode; equal areas also test the next antipode. Two-point\/collinear hulls need one pair test. Distance uses widened hypot and narrows only the final finite scalar. Ties retain the first encountered represented distance, so an equally far pair can differ from the historical exhaustive scan. Hull O(N log N), caliper walk O(H) area\/pair tests plus the exact predicate constant; working\/output O(N+H), optional O(H) events. Complete finite inputs required; at least two distinct points. Inputs unchanged and results owned. Counters exclude hull construction\/validation and predicate internal arithmetic.
