-- | Cressie–Read power-divergence goodness-of-fit test for specified probabilities.
--
-- Power 1 gives Pearson\'s statistic, 0 the likelihood-ratio G statistic, and -1 its reverse. A zero observed count is treated by continuity and yields an infinite divergence when power is at most -1. Uses an asymptotic chi-square reference.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto fit = dm::stats::power_divergence_test({25, 15}, {.5, .5}, 1);
-- > std::print("{:.1f}\n", fit.statistic); // 2.5
