-- Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: @estimated\_parameters@ = @0@.
--
-- C++: @HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::power\_divergence\_test(const std::vector\<double\> & observed, const std::vector\<double\> & expected\_probabilities = {}, double power = 0.0, std::size\_t estimated\_parameters = 0)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Invalid counts, probabilities, power or degrees of freedom.
--
-- See also: 'chiSquaredGoodnessOfFit'.
