-- | Pearson chi-square test for a contingency table, like R chisq.test().
--
-- Expected counts are row\_sum/column\_sum\/total; df=(rows-1)(columns-1). The asymptotic reference assumes independent multinomial\/product-multinomial observations and adequately populated expected cells. O(rows/columns) work and O(rows+columns) space; inputs unchanged, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto q=dm::stats::chi_squared_test_independence({10,10,10,10},2,2);
-- > std::print("{:.0f}\n",q.statistic); // 0
