chiSquaredTestIndependenceWithCorrect _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 = R.call 204 [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.toCpp _x4] P.>>= R.result

-- | Pearson product-moment correlation test with Fisher-z confidence bounds.
--
-- Uses t=r\*sqrt((n-2)\/(1-r^2)). The exact zero-correlation null reference requires independent bivariate-normal pairs; Fisher-z intervals are approximate. At n=3 no confidence interval is reported; n\>=4 gets one. Perfect correlations use infinite-statistic limits. O(n) work, no input mutation\/omission or shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto r=dm::stats::pearson_correlation_test({1,2,3,4},{2,4,6,8});
-- > std::print("{:.1f}\n",r.estimate1); // 1.0
