-- | Conditional Fisher exact test of a 2x2 table with fixed margins.
--
-- Conditions on row\/column totals and tests odds ratio one. Two-sided p-values sum probabilities no larger than the observed table (relative ordering tolerance 1e-7); they are not generally twice the smaller tail. Direct tail summation avoids 1-CDF cancellation. Empty margins give p=1. O(s) work\/O(1) auxiliary storage for feasible support s; inputs unchanged, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto f=dm::stats::fisher_exact_test_2x2(0,3,3,0);
-- > std::print("{:.1f}\n",f.p_value); // 0.1
--
-- __References__
--
-- * https:\/\/stat.ethz.ch\/R-manual\/R-devel\/library\/stats\/html\/fisher.test.html
--
-- Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: @alternative@ = @AlternativeTwoSided@.
--
-- C++: @HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::fisher\_exact\_test\_2x2(std::size\_t a, std::size\_t b, std::size\_t c, std::size\_t d, Alternative alternative = TwoSided)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Count-total overflow or invalid alternative.
--
-- See also: 'HypothesisTestResult'.
fisherExactTest2x2
  :: P.Int  -- ^ Top-left nonnegative integer count.
  -> P.Int  -- ^ Top-right count.
  -> P.Int  -- ^ Bottom-left count.
  -> P.Int  -- ^ Bottom-right count; total must fit size\_t.
  -> P.IO HypothesisTestResult  -- ^ statistic=a, p\_value and estimate1=sample odds ratio a/d\/(b/c), not R conditional MLE; denominator zero gives infinity for positive numerator or NaN for 0\/0. No confidence interval.
fisherExactTest2x2 _x1 _x2 _x3 _x4 = R.call 208 [R.toCpp _x1, R.toCpp _x2, R.toCpp _x3, R.toCpp _x4] P.>>= R.result

-- | Conditional Fisher exact test of a 2x2 table with fixed margins.
