-- | Two-sample KS comparison of empirical CDFs with asymptotic p-values.
--
-- Uses effective n=n\_x\*n\_y\/(n\_x+n\_y) in the asymptotic reference. This is not an exact finite- sample calculation; ties\/rounding and very small groups affect calibration. O(N log N) work\/O(N) storage; inputs unchanged, no omission\/shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto k=dm::stats::ks_test_two_sample({1,2,3},{1,2,3});
-- > std::print("{:.0f}\n",k.statistic); // 0
