-- | Pooled score test for two proportions, with an unpooled difference interval.
--
-- Tests equality using the pooled null SE and optionally a capped continuity correction. The difference CI uses an unpooled Wald SE and an uncapped half-count width correction when requested; it is approximate and is not a Wilson\/Newcombe interval. All-zero\/all-one pooled samples return z=0,p=1. O(1) work\/storage, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto p=dm::stats::proportion_test_two_sample(2,10,3,10);
-- > std::print("{:.1f}\n",p.estimate1); // 0.2
--
-- __References__
