-- | Exact binomial test with Clopper-Pearson confidence bounds, like R binom.test().
--
-- One-sided p-values are inclusive tails. Two-sided p-values sum PMFs no larger than the observed PMF, using relative comparison tolerance 1e-7. The equal-tailed Clopper-Pearson interval has at-least-nominal coverage but need not invert the probability-ordered two-sided test. Null endpoints zero\/one are supported. Two-sided enumeration costs O(n), intervals use bounded beta-CDF bisection; O(1) auxiliary storage, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto b=dm::stats::binomial_test(9,10);
-- > std::print("{:.6f}\n",b.p_value); // 0.021484
--
-- __References__
--
-- * https:\/\/stat.ethz.ch\/R-manual\/R-devel\/library\/stats\/html\/binom.test.html
