-- | Normal-approximation Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie\/continuity corrections.
--
-- Tests symmetry of x-mu about zero under independent observations, not an arbitrary-population mean or median null. For paired data pass aligned differences. Exact-zero differences are removed; absolute differences receive average ranks. Always uses a normal approximation, even for small tie-free samples; no exact option or CI. O(n log n) work\/O(n) storage; input unchanged, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test({1,2,3,4});
-- > std::print("{:.0f}\n",w.statistic); // 10
--
-- __References__
--
-- * https:\/\/stat.ethz.ch\/R-manual\/R-devel\/library\/stats\/html\/wilcox.test.html
--
-- Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: @mu@ = @0.0@, @alternative@ = @AlternativeTwoSided@.
--
-- C++: @HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::wilcoxon\_signed\_rank\_test(const std::vector\<double\> & x, double mu = 0.0, Alternative alternative = TwoSided)@
--
-- Throws t'R.CppError' ('R.InvalidArgument') for C++ @std::invalid\_argument@: Nonfinite input\/mu, invalid alternative, no nonzero differences or zero rank variance.
--
-- See also: 'HypothesisTestResult'.
wilcoxonSignedRankTest
  :: [P.Double]  -- ^ Finite values; at least one nonzero difference from mu must remain.
  -> P.IO HypothesisTestResult  -- ^ statistic=positive rank sum V, estimate1=mu (not an estimated pseudomedian), approximate p\_value; no CI.
wilcoxonSignedRankTest _x1 = R.call 226 [R.toCpp _x1] P.>>= R.result

-- | Normal-approximation Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie\/continuity corrections.
--
-- Tests symmetry of x-mu about zero under independent observations, not an arbitrary-population mean or median null. For paired data pass aligned differences. Exact-zero differences are removed; absolute differences receive average ranks. Always uses a normal approximation, even for small tie-free samples; no exact option or CI. O(n log n) work\/O(n) storage; input unchanged, no shared state.
--
-- __Example__
--
-- > const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test({1,2,3,4});
-- > std::print("{:.0f}\n",w.statistic); // 10
