-- | Create a directory and any missing parent directories. Accepts native filesystem paths, strings and string literals. An existing directory is a successful no-op; an existing file at the target or along its parents is an error. Relative paths use the current working directory, which this function does not change. Permissions follow the native filesystem and process defaults. A failed recursive operation may leave created parents. This C++ convenience forwards to std::filesystem::create\_directories().
